From 1a6cbd62a9ea8d5c8f7c7625490bcec227e799ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?L=C6=B0u=20Oa=20Oa?=
 <212658678+luuoaoa@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 11:30:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Region-neutral build: the language is data, not a compiled-in
 default

ApplyColorburstLocalAccountDefaults() pinned --cros-region=vn, which made
the OOBE language a property of the Chrome binary. Shipping a second
language would have meant a second full Chrome build of an otherwise
byte-identical OS -- hours of compile for one string.

Move the region out of the binary. session_manager now reads it from the
OEM partition and passes --cros-region explicitly
(login_manager/chrome_setup.cc, AddColorburstRegionFlag), so one build
serves every variant and a USB image's language is chosen by rewriting a
16 MiB partition that carries neither verity nor a signature. That
partition is the only one that survives install, OTA and powerwash
alike, so a device also keeps the personality of the stick it came from.

The fallback here stays, flipped vn -> us, for a Chrome started outside
session_manager (ash by hand, a browser test) where nothing supplies a
region. It matches what an unrepacked image gives you: English. Because
session_manager always passes the switch and this is add-if-absent, the
fallback never fires on a real boot -- which is also why the variant
plumbing works on an image built before this patch.

Vietnamese is now a variant (region=vn) rather than the default. Nothing
Vietnamese is lost: the IME, the Telex/VNI/VIQR methods and the vi
translations all live in the same image and switch on with the locale.
---
 chrome/app/chrome_main_delegate.cc | 19 ++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chrome/app/chrome_main_delegate.cc b/chrome/app/chrome_main_delegate.cc
index a8aa682ba2..a47b37cb56 100644
--- a/chrome/app/chrome_main_delegate.cc
+++ b/chrome/app/chrome_main_delegate.cc
@@ -1119,12 +1119,21 @@ void ApplyColorburstLocalAccountDefaults() {
       command_line->AppendSwitch(flag);
     }
   }
-  // Vietnamese by default: cros-regions.json carries a "vn" entry, and
-  // --cros-region overrides the VPD region, which generic hardware does not
-  // have. Gives Vietnamese OOBE, Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh and the Vietnamese keyboard
-  // layouts.
+  // The region is deliberately NOT set here any more. It used to be pinned to
+  // "vn", which made the language a property of the binary: shipping a second
+  // language meant a second 4-hour Chrome build of an otherwise identical OS.
+  //
+  // colorburst is region-neutral now. session_manager reads the region off the
+  // OEM partition and passes --cros-region (login_manager/chrome_setup.cc,
+  // AddColorburstRegionFlag), so one build serves every variant and a USB
+  // image's language is set by rewriting a 16 MiB unsigned partition.
+  //
+  // This fallback stays as the last line of defence for a Chrome started
+  // outside session_manager -- a developer running ash by hand, a browser test
+  // -- where nothing has supplied a region. English, matching an image whose
+  // OEM partition is empty.
   if (!command_line->HasSwitch(ash::switches::kCrosRegion)) {
-    command_line->AppendSwitchASCII(ash::switches::kCrosRegion, "vn");
+    command_line->AppendSwitchASCII(ash::switches::kCrosRegion, "us");
   }
 }
 
